Phase 3 charging bring-up (2026-09-20, docs/phase3-battery-scoping.md,
docs/kernel-boot-debugging.md): mainline's MAX77705 MFD probe
(drivers/mfd/max77705.c) only accepted MAX77705_PASS3 silicon,
rejecting anything else as "Rev.0x%x is not tested". This project's
real Samsung Galaxy Tab S7 LTE unit reports PASS2 (confirmed via a
clean regmap read of the revision register - a genuine I2C success,
not a mis-wiring or bus problem).

Samsung's own downstream driver (references/gts7l/drivers/mfd/
max77705.c and max77705-irq.c) treats PASS2 as a fully normal,
supported revision throughout - every switch-case that branches on
chip revision handles PASS2 identically to PASS3, never as a rejected
or special-cased stepping. This confirms the upstream gate is simply
more conservative than real shipped hardware (most likely because
whoever wrote/tested the mainline driver only had PASS3 silicon on
hand), not evidence of a genuine incompatibility.

Relaxes the check to accept both PASS2 and PASS3, rather than
disabling or bypassing the revision check entirely - keeps the
protection against a genuinely wrong/unexpected chip revision while
allowing this project's real hardware to probe. Same precedent as this
project's existing drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c patch (0003): a small,
well-justified upstream driver change for a real, confirmed hardware
fact, not a workaround for a DTS mistake.

Applies on top of Linux 7.2 with 0002-0004 already applied.

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/max77705.c b/drivers/mfd/max77705.c
index e98c76d6b..dac60dd95 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/max77705.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/max77705.c
@@ -104,8 +104,20 @@ static int max77705_i2c_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return -ENODEV;

+	/*
+	 * gts7l (docs/phase3-battery-scoping.md, docs/kernel-boot-debugging.md):
+	 * real hardware (Samsung Galaxy Tab S7 LTE) reports PASS2 here, not
+	 * PASS3 - confirmed via a clean regmap read (this project's chip
+	 * genuinely is PASS2, not a mis-wiring). Samsung's own downstream
+	 * driver (references/gts7l/drivers/mfd/max77705.c/-irq.c) treats
+	 * PASS2 as a fully normal, supported revision throughout (handled
+	 * identically to PASS3 in every switch-case seen), not a rejected
+	 * or unsupported stepping - this upstream check is simply more
+	 * conservative than real shipped hardware, not evidence of a real
+	 * incompatibility.
+	 */
 	pmic_rev = pmic_rev_value & MAX77705_REVISION_MASK;
-	if (pmic_rev != MAX77705_PASS3)
+	if (pmic_rev != MAX77705_PASS2 && pmic_rev != MAX77705_PASS3)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, -ENODEV, "Rev.0x%x is not tested\n", pmic_rev);

 	/* Active Discharge Enable */
